GFOSFonts 1.0 (14.11.2026)
==========================

GFOS's own screen fonts: GFOS Sans, GFOS Sans Bold and GFOS Mono, bitmap fonts
corrected by hand pixel by pixel, each in 11, 13 and 16 pixels, for FONTS:.
They cover ISO-Latin-1 ($20-$7E and $A0-$FF); $7F-$9F draw an empty box.

Source:  https://github.com/DalsinAI/gfosfonts
Version: 1.0, 14 November 2026


The nine fonts
--------------

  Font file              Sizes         What
  GFOSSans.font          11, 13, 16    GFOS Sans, proportional
  GFOSSansBold.font      11, 13, 16    GFOS Sans Bold, proportional, 2 pixel stems
                                       drawn into the font (not a smeared Regular)
  GFOSMono.font          11, 13, 16    GFOS Mono, fixed width: 7, 8 and 10 pixels
                                       wide, for the Shell, code and columns

The 13 is the size made for most screens, the 11 for low resolution screens and
the 16 for large ones. Pick them in Font prefs (SYS:Prefs/Font) or in any program
that asks for a font.


What is in this archive
-----------------------

  Fonts/        the fonts, laid out exactly as they go into FONTS:
                (GFOSSans.font and the drawer GFOSSans/ with 11, 13 and 16,
                and the same for GFOSSansBold and GFOSMono)
  Specimens/    the specimen sheets, as PNG pictures
  Install       a Shell script that copies the fonts to FONTS:
  ReadMe        this file
  LICENSE-FONTS the fonts' licence (the Bitstream Vera licence)
  LICENSE-TOOLS the licence of the gfosfonts tools that built them (MIT)
  SHA256SUMS    the SHA-256 of every other file here


Installing
----------

With the Install script, from a Shell:

    CD GFOSFonts-1.0
    Execute Install

It copies each of the three fonts to FONTS: unless a font of the same name is
already there (FONTS:GFOSSans.font or the drawer FONTS:GFOSSans, and so on).
A font that is already there is left as it is and named, so a font you have
is never replaced without you asking. To replace it:

    Execute Install FORCE

which first copies the old .font file and drawer into the drawer Old/ beside
the Install script, then puts this release's in their place. The new .font
lists 11, 13 and 16 only; any other size you had in that drawer stays in it
(and in Old/) but is no longer listed.

By hand, from a Shell:

    Copy GFOSFonts-1.0/Fonts/#? FONTS: ALL CLONE

or copy the contents of Fonts/ to FONTS: with a file manager. Don't run
FixFonts on them: the .font files here are already right.

With GFOpenUp: GFOpenUp installs these same fonts (its GFOSFonts part, 1.0)
with every install, and leaves a font of the same name that another program
put there alone. The font files in this archive are byte for byte the ones
GFOpenUp's GFOSFonts 1.0 part installs.

Nothing here changes Font prefs: the fonts are offered, not made the
system's fonts.


Licence and where the fonts come from
-------------------------------------

The fonts are derived from DejaVu Sans 2.37 (https://dejavu-fonts.github.io/),
which is based on Bitstream Vera, Copyright (c) 2003 by Bitstream, Inc. All
Rights Reserved. Bitstream Vera is a trademark of Bitstream, Inc. DejaVu's
changes are in the public domain. Our changes are under the same licence:
the Bitstream Vera licence, in LICENSE-FONTS, which must go with every copy.
As that licence requires for changed fonts, these are renamed: GFOS Sans,
GFOS Sans Bold and GFOS Mono.

The tools in the gfosfonts repository that build these files (gridfont.py,
amigafont.py, dump_grid.c) are under the MIT licence, in LICENSE-TOOLS.

